Below is the change description:
The primary motivation is to align the Spring AI Mistral connector with the evolving Mistral AI API capabilities. Specifically, the introduction of 'reasoning' models requires new request parameters like 'reasoning_effort'. Furthermore, the API has introduced advanced multi-modal and structured content features (such as citations, references, and chain-of-thought 'thinking' processes), which necessitated a more robust and flexible way to serialize and deserialize message content beyond simple strings, hence the migration to structured content chunks.
The changes significantly update the Mistral AI integration in Spring AI. Key updates include: adding support for reasoning models via the new 'ReasoningEffort' parameter in options and requests; enhanced support for complex content structures in ChatCompletionMessage, now using a sealed interface (ContentChunk) to handle Text, ImageUrl, Thinking, and Reference types with custom Jackson serialization; improved handling of metadata extraction for thinking and reference content; updated MistralAiApi models for better compatibility with newer API features; and addition of new integration tests to verify these capabilities.

